# Datasheet for BBO Capstone Project

## Dataset Overview
The dataset used in this project comes from a black-box optimisation (BBO) environment provided as part of the capstone challenge. The objective was to optimise multiple unknown functions (F1–F8) with very limited observations.

## Data Collection Process
Data was collected iteratively over 13 weeks. At each iteration, a new input vector was submitted and the corresponding output value was returned. This process simulates real-world scenarios where data is expensive and must be acquired sequentially.

## Data Characteristics

- High uncertainty due to unknown function structure
- Potential noise in function evaluations
- Multi-dimensional inputs (varying across functions)

## Limitations
- The true form of the underlying functions is unknown
- Sparse data makes it difficult to fully capture global structure
- Some functions exhibit unstable or noisy behaviour
- Results may not be reproducible due to stochastic elements

## Bias and Risks
- Early samples may bias the model toward suboptimal regions
- Overfitting is a risk due to small sample size
- Exploration-exploitation trade-off may lead to incomplete coverage of the search space

## Intended Use
This dataset is intended for experimentation with optimisation strategies, particularly Bayesian Optimisation techniques, in low-data and high-uncertainty environments.

## Not Intended Use
The dataset is not suitable for:
- Supervised learning tasks with large datasets
- Generalisation to real-world systems without further validation
